{"type":"text","timestamp":1785674165004,"sessionID":"ses_03d875b74ffexQhILnNH8GIzQQ","part":{"id":"prt_fc2796735001ZTT0NNmCRhGWDa","messageID":"msg_fc2795e56001ZY2shISKPoHtXA","sessionID":"ses_03d875b74ffexQhILnNH8GIzQQ","type":"text","text":"The oldest SJS patient is Patient ID 125619 (Birthday 1917-04-18, the smallest among SJS patients). Their most recent laboratory work was completed on 1986-01-07, and their age when initially arriving at the hospital was 1986 − 1917 = 69 years old.\n\nFinal Answer: Medical laboratory work completed on 1986-01-07; age at initial arrival 69 years\nEvidence SQL: SELECT p.ID, MAX(l.Date) AS Latest_Lab_Date, strftime('%Y', p.\"First Date\") - strftime('%Y', p.Birthday) AS Age_At_Arrival FROM Patient p JOIN Laboratory l ON p.ID = l.ID WHERE p.Diagnosis='SJS' AND p.Birthday = (SELECT MIN(Birthday) FROM Patient WHERE Diagnosis='SJS')","time":{"start":1785674164021,"end":1785674164993}}}
